IONetworkingFamily for Minkar
==============================

Our own implementation (BSD-2-Clause) of the macOS network driver family:
IONetworkController, IOEthernetController, IONetworkInterface,
IOEthernetInterface, IONetworkMedium and the output queues
(IOBasicOutputQueue, IOGatedOutputQueue). It follows the public API of
macOS 10.15 so that drivers written for it build here; it is not binary
compatible with Apple's kext, and contains no Apple code.

The bundle identifier is com.apple.iokit.IONetworkingFamily, the name
drivers list in OSBundleLibraries.

How it works:

* A driver calls attachInterface(); registering the interface creates and
  attaches its ifnet with the XNU interface KPI (ifnet_allocate, legacy
  output model), names it prefix + unit (en0, en1, ... in registration
  order) and attaches BPF.
* IFF_UP and IFF_DOWN call the controller's enable() and disable() inside
  its command gate. Packets from the stack go to the controller's output
  queue; kIOReturnOutputStall keeps the packet until service().
* inputPacket() strips the link-level header the way the stack wants it
  and hands packets to ifnet_input(), one at a time or in batches
  (kInputOptionQueuePacket + flushInputQueue()).
* setLinkStatus() posts KEV_DL_LINK_ON/OFF; SIOCGIFMEDIA reports the
  active medium and link status (not the list of media).

Not implemented yet: IONetworkStack (persistent unit numbers), IOKernelDebugger,
IONetworkData statistics, checksum and TSO offload, VLANs, power management,
the IONetworkUserClient.
